# requirements/data-sources/archives.ears
capability: Archive access and acquisition
owner: data-sources
requirements:
  - id: DSI-001
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The system shall access every archive only through ArchiveGateway with a declared dialect per source release."
    rationale: "One port, one canonical schema, one declared dialect per source (§8)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T0, T3]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.archives.test_dialects::test_a_release_without_a_dialect_cannot_be_curated"
      - "python/tests.archives.test_tap::test_every_packaged_source_declares_licence_citation_limits_and_a_dialect"
  - id: DSI-002
    pattern: event
    text: "When a dataset is acquired, the system shall record the rendered query text, source release, licence, citation, checksum, byte count and timestamp."
    rationale: "Every acquisition is auditable and replayable."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.contract.test_kernel_fakes.TestArchiveGateway::test_query_renders_text_and_a_stable_idempotency_key"
      - "python/tests.usecase.test_acquire_dataset::test_acquisition_records_query_release_licence_citation_checksum_size_and_time"
  - id: DSI-003
    pattern: unwanted
    text: "If a downloaded chunk fails checksum verification, then the system shall discard it, emit DatasetRejected and retry within the bounded policy."
    rationale: "A corrupted chunk must never become evidence."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T5]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.usecase.test_acquire_dataset::test_corrupted_chunk_is_discarded_rejected_and_retried"
      - "python/tests.usecase.test_acquire_dataset::test_retries_are_bounded"
  - id: DSI-004
    pattern: event
    text: "When an acquisition repeats an existing idempotency key, the system shall return the existing artifact without a remote call."
    rationale: "Repeat acquisitions are free and identical."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.contract.test_kernel_fakes.TestDatasetRepository::test_find_by_idempotency_key"
      - "python/tests.usecase.test_acquire_dataset::test_repeated_idempotency_key_returns_existing_artifact_without_a_remote_call"
  - id: DSI-007
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The CI pipeline shall run archive adapter contract tests from recorded cassettes without a live archive call."
    rationale: "Live archives are rate-limited and change (ADR-015)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T5]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.archives.test_tap::test_replay_never_falls_back_to_the_network"
      - "python/tests.archives.test_transport::test_a_missing_cassette_is_an_error_not_a_live_call"
      - "python/tests.archives.test_wiring::test_replay_mode_puts_every_gateway_on_cassettes"
  - id: DSI-008
    pattern: event
    text: "When the weekly live smoke detects a column added, renamed or retyped, the system shall fail the job and name the column."
    rationale: "Schema drift is caught within a week."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T11]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.archives.test_smoke::test_the_smoke_records_then_fails_on_drift_naming_the_column"
      - "python/tests.archives.test_xmatch_drift_duckdb::test_drift_names_every_added_removed_and_retyped_column"
  - id: DSI-011
    pattern: event
    text: "When a catalogue query covers a cone of 0.5 degrees radius or more, the system shall bound the cone's ADQL with an RA and Dec range that holds the whole cone."
    rationale: "The Gaia archive times out on CONTAINS alone beyond about 1 degree; the same circle behind a BETWEEN range answers in seconds (#58)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.archives.test_tap::test_a_wide_cone_puts_a_bounding_box_in_front_of_contains"
      - "python/tests.archives.test_tap::test_the_bounding_box_always_holds_the_whole_circle"
  - id: DSI-012
    pattern: event
    text: "When a catalogue read returns as many rows as its row cap, the system shall report the source and cap with the acquisition and in the summary of every Investigate stage that read it."
    rationale: "A query is TOP row_cap in key order, so a capped read keeps one patch of the field and drops the rest; the scientist must know (#59)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3, T4]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.usecase.test_acquire_dataset::test_an_acquisition_that_fills_its_row_cap_says_so"
      - "python/tests.usecase.test_investigate::test_a_stage_whose_read_filled_its_row_cap_names_the_source"
  - id: DSI-013
    pattern: event
    text: "When a bulk sweep stores a publisher file, the system shall verify the file against the published MD5, keep only the source's declared columns with their declared types, and skip every file already stored on a later run."
    rationale: "All of Gaia DR3 is about 3,400 files and days of downloading; a sweep must be resumable, verified and no wider than what SDP reads (#72)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.archives.test_bulk::test_each_file_becomes_a_typed_parquet_of_the_declared_columns_with_its_record"
      - "python/tests.archives.test_bulk::test_a_rerun_skips_stored_files_and_a_bad_md5_fails_only_that_file"
      - "python/tests.archives.test_bulk::test_the_sweep_stops_at_the_disk_floor_before_downloading"
  - id: DSI-014
    pattern: state
    text: "While a complete bulk copy of a source release is stored, the system shall answer that source's catalogue queries from the copy with the rows, column types, order, row cap and chunks the archive query would return, under rendered query text marked as a bulk read."
    rationale: "Once all of Gaia is on disk, runs read fields locally with no TAP call; an incomplete copy would silently drop stars, so it is never read unless asked for, and then it is refused (#72)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.archives.test_bulk_read::test_a_cone_returns_exactly_the_stars_inside_it_ordered_by_source_id"
      - "python/tests.archives.test_bulk_read::test_a_box_is_plain_betweens_and_the_filters_apply_as_in_adql"
      - "python/tests.archives.test_bulk_read::test_the_row_cap_and_chunks_page_as_the_archive_does"
      - "python/tests.archives.test_bulk_read::test_an_empty_field_is_one_empty_batch_of_the_declared_columns"
      - "python/tests.archives.test_bulk_read::test_the_query_text_is_marked_bulk_so_its_dataset_never_passes_for_an_archive_read"
      - "python/tests.archives.test_bulk_read::test_an_incomplete_copy_is_refused_and_auto_keeps_the_archive"
  - id: DSI-015
    pattern: event
    text: "When the system fetches a known-cluster catalogue, the system shall fill each benchmark column from the service column whose UCD and unit match it, refuse a catalogue lacking a required column, and record the release, licence, citation and chosen columns with the stored table."
    rationale: "VizieR names columns after each paper; choosing by UCD and checking the unit keeps a column in arcsec/yr or an error column out of the proper-motion window of the UC-01 cross-match (STL-005)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3, T4]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.archives.test_benchmarks::test_columns_are_chosen_by_ucd_and_never_by_an_error_column"
      - "python/tests.archives.test_benchmarks::test_a_column_in_another_unit_is_refused_by_name"
      - "python/tests.archives.test_benchmarks::test_a_fetched_catalogue_is_a_benchmark_the_cross_match_accepts"
      - "python/tests.cli.test_cli_benchmark::test_fetch_stores_both_catalogues_and_prints_the_input_to_define_with"
  - id: DSI-016
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The system shall curate a whole native table column by column with the same canonical output, exclusions and refusals as curating it row by row."
    rationale: "Row-by-row curation of the 216 GB local Gaia copy would take days; the columnar path makes the sky sweep feasible only if it can never disagree with the audited row path."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.archives.test_dialect_columnar::test_every_packaged_dialect_curates_its_golden_rows_identically"
      - "python/tests.archives.test_dialect_columnar::test_a_blank_declination_leaves_the_ra_motion_as_the_row_path_does"
      - "python/tests.archives.test_dialect_columnar::test_gaia_rows_with_nulls_curate_identically_and_faster"
      - "python/tests.archives.test_dialect_columnar::test_rows_without_an_epoch_are_excluded_and_counted_as_the_row_path_does"
      - "python/tests.archives.test_dialect_columnar::test_a_native_table_lacking_a_column_is_refused_by_name"
  - id: DSI-017
    pattern: event
    text: "When TAPVizieR gives no answer or a server error for a known-cluster catalogue, the system shall read the same table from the first VizieR mirror that answers, or from a VOTable file the user saved, choosing its columns by the UCDs and units its fields carry, refusing a VOTable whose first table is not that catalogue, and record which service or file it came from."
    rationale: "CDS outages blocked the UC-01 benchmarks for a day (#107); VizieR's mirrors and its saved VOTables describe every column with the same UCDs, so the DSI-015 checks still hold, while a refusal (a 4xx, a VOTable whose QUERY_STATUS is ERROR, or a missing column) is never papered over by asking elsewhere, and a saved file of another catalogue never becomes this benchmark."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3, T4]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.archives.test_benchmarks::test_when_tapvizier_gives_no_answer_the_first_mirror_that_answers_serves_the_same_benchmark"
      - "python/tests.archives.test_benchmarks::test_the_mirror_query_asks_for_the_whole_table_in_decimal_degrees"
      - "python/tests.archives.test_benchmarks::test_a_server_error_moves_on_but_a_refusal_does_not"
      - "python/tests.archives.test_benchmarks::test_when_nothing_answers_every_service_tried_is_named"
      - "python/tests.archives.test_benchmarks::test_a_saved_votable_reads_its_units_as_written_and_becomes_the_same_benchmark"
      - "python/tests.cli.test_cli_benchmark::test_a_saved_votable_is_stored_without_any_download"
      - "python/tests.cli.test_cli_benchmark::test_a_file_of_another_catalogue_is_not_stored_under_this_one"
      - "python/tests.archives.test_benchmarks::test_a_votable_of_another_or_an_unnamed_table_is_refused"
      - "python/tests.archives.test_benchmarks::test_a_query_a_mirror_refuses_in_its_votable_is_not_asked_elsewhere"
      - "python/tests.archives.test_benchmarks::test_a_mirror_reply_cut_off_in_its_rows_moves_on_to_the_next_mirror"
  - id: DSI-021
    pattern: optional
    text: "Where a bulk subset is requested, the system shall store, beside the full copy, only the rows of each verified publisher file whose subset key column has a value, with the parent source's declared columns and the subset's declared columns, for a gateway over that subset copy to read."
    rationale: "Oort's 1932 disc density needs radial velocities, which the full Gaia copy does not keep. Gaia DR3 gives one for about 33.8 million of its 1.8 billion stars (ESA gaia_source data model, read 2026-10-31), so keeping those rows alone costs a few GB, and the full copy's columns, and every existing reader of it, stay as they are."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.archives.test_bulk_subset::test_the_rvs_subset_declares_the_radial_velocity_columns_with_the_types_esa_publishes"
      - "python/tests.archives.test_bulk_subset::test_only_stars_with_a_radial_velocity_are_kept_beside_the_full_copy"
      - "python/tests.archives.test_bulk_subset::test_the_rvs_gateway_reads_a_field_with_its_radial_velocities"
      - "python/tests.archives.test_bulk_subset::test_a_subset_cannot_redeclare_a_parent_column_or_keep_rows_by_a_column_it_lacks"
      - "python/tests.archives.test_bulk_subset::test_the_cli_builds_the_rvs_subset_and_refuses_an_unknown_one"
      - "python/tests.archives.test_bulk_subset::test_a_subset_read_never_shares_its_query_text_or_key_with_the_full_copy"
      - "python/tests.archives.test_bulk_subset::test_a_subset_field_can_be_ordered_by_a_column_it_does_not_select"
      - "python/tests.archives.test_bulk_subset::test_a_subset_name_is_one_plain_path_segment"
  - id: DSI-022
    pattern: event
    text: "When a whole-sky scan of a complete bulk copy is requested, the system shall return each stored file in turn with only the requested columns and only the rows that pass every requested filter."
    rationale: "UC-04 fits the whole sky; one file in memory at a time with Parquet pushdown keeps a pass over 1.8 billion stars within a desktop's memory, and an incomplete copy is refused as in DSI-014."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T4]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.cli.test_cli_oort1927::test_a_scan_reads_every_file_with_its_filters_and_refuses_an_incomplete_copy"
